//@version=6
indicator("MACD + Impulse MACD - Normalized Momentum Scale", "MACD", overlay=false, max_bars_back=5000, calc_bars_count=1500, max_labels_count=100, max_lines_count=50)



// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Script Overview
// ==============================================================================================
//
// MACD + IMPULSE — NORMALIZED MOMENTUM SCALE
//
// WHAT THIS INDICATOR IS
// • This indicator places standard Price MACD and Impulse MACD on one shared, volatility-normalized
//   -100…+100 coordinate so their direction, crossover structure, histogram strength, and higher-timeframe
//   context can be compared without relying on their unrelated native price-unit scales.
// • Standard Price MACD uses the familiar 12 / 26 / 9 architecture by default, with user-adjustable
//   Fast / Slow / Signal lengths.
// • Impulse MACD uses a 34-period smoothed High/Low envelope around a 34-period zero-lag EMA midline,
//   with a 9-period Signal by default; its MA / Signal lengths are also user-adjustable.
// • The Impulse MACD implementation is inspired by LazyBear's public Impulse MACD:
//      https://www.tradingview.com/v/qt6xLfLi/
//
//
// PRIOR WORK / ATTRIBUTION
// • Volatility-normalized MACD has important prior published work in Alex Spiroglou's
//   "MACD-V: Volatility Normalised Momentum" (2022).
// • Original MACD-V TradingView publication:
//      https://www.tradingview.com/script/mMMHCZUx-AS-MACD-v-Hist-Alex-Spiroglou-S-M-A-R-T-TRADER-SYSTEMS/
// • MACD-V uses a linear ATR-normalized MACD architecture built around:
//      MACD → divide by ATR26 → ×100 → EMA normalized series → histogram.
// • This script uses a materially different order of operations:
//      raw MACD + raw classic Signal + raw classic Histogram
//      → independently divide each by ATR14
//      → independently map each through the nonlinear bounded Normalized Momentum Scale.
// • In practical terms, this script preserves the conventional raw MACD / Signal relationship first,
//   then expresses MACD, Signal, and the true raw Histogram on a common volatility-relative coordinate.
// • MACD-V and its research remain the work of Alex Spiroglou; the attribution above recognizes that
//   prior work in volatility-normalized MACD while distinguishing the implementation used here.
// • The Impulse MACD implementation is separately inspired by LazyBear's public Impulse MACD:
//      https://www.tradingview.com/v/qt6xLfLi/
//
// WHY USE A NORMALIZED MOMENTUM SCALE?
// • Native MACD values are expressed in price units. That creates three practical problems:
//      1) the same raw MACD number means something very different on a $20 stock, a $500 stock, or crypto;
//      2) the same instrument naturally produces different MACD magnitudes on different timeframes;
//      3) standard MACD and Impulse MACD are built from different geometry, so their raw magnitudes are
//         not directly comparable even when both are describing momentum.
// • The first step is therefore ATR14 normalization:
//      raw momentum value ÷ ATR14.
// • This converts each reading from raw price distance into units of prevailing volatility. A reading is
//   no longer asking "how many dollars apart are these averages?" but rather "how large is this momentum
//   displacement relative to the instrument's current volatility?"
//
// NORMALIZED MOMENTUM SCALE (NMS)
// • ATR normalization solves the price-unit problem, but a simple linear plot still creates a display problem.
//   If the pane is scaled to preserve rare large excursions, ordinary MACD movement gets compressed around zero.
//   If it is scaled for ordinary movement, occasional large momentum expansions dominate the pane.
// • The Normalized Momentum Scale solves that tradeoff with a monotonic nonlinear transfer from ATR-relative
//   momentum into a bounded -100…+100 coordinate.
// • The center of the scale intentionally receives more visual resolution, while increasingly uncommon
//   volatility-relative expansion requires progressively larger raw movement to approach the outer levels.
// • Fixed absolute-value reference anchors are:
//      0.00 ATR → 0
//      0.70 ATR → 34
//      1.25 ATR → 55
//      2.50 ATR → 65
//      4.00 ATR → 75
//      7.00 ATR → 89
//      12.0 ATR → 95
//      20.0 ATR → 100
// • Positive values indicate positive signed momentum displacement; negative values indicate negative displacement.
// • These values are NOT probabilities, percentages, or automatic overbought / oversold signals. They are a
//   standardized description of signed momentum magnitude relative to volatility.
//
// WHY THIS WORKS FOR MACD / SIGNAL PAIRS
// • MACD and its Signal are each normalized by the same ATR14 denominator on the same bar and then passed through
//   the same monotonic NMS transfer.
// • Because the transfer preserves ordering, MACD / Signal crossover ownership is preserved while both lines gain
//   a standardized coordinate.
// • The same treatment is applied independently to Impulse MACD and its Signal.
// • This lets the user compare not only which line is leading, but also how far the entire pair has migrated
//   through a common volatility-relative momentum range.
//
// HISTOGRAMS ARE MAPPED FROM THEIR TRUE RAW DIFFERENCE
// • Standard MACD Histogram is:
//      raw MACD − raw MACD Signal.
// • Impulse Hist is:
//      raw Impulse MACD − raw Impulse Signal.
// • Each true raw histogram is divided by ATR14 and passed through NMS independently.
// • The histogram is intentionally NOT calculated by subtracting the two already-normalized NMS lines.
//   Subtracting values after a nonlinear transfer would distort the magnitude of the original histogram.
// • Standard MACD Hist uses the MACD pair color:
//      positive = teal;
//      negative = Bear Fall magenta.
// • Impulse Hist uses a separate visual palette:
//      positive = orange;
//      negative = light purple.
//
// STANDARD MACD + IMPULSE MACD TOGETHER
// • Standard MACD responds directly to the relationship between two exponential averages of Close.
// • Impulse MACD adds a different perspective: its zero-lag EMA midline must extend beyond a smoothed High/Low
//   envelope before the raw Impulse value moves away from zero.
// • Putting both on the same NMS coordinate makes their differences useful rather than confusing.
// • Agreement can show momentum that is being expressed by both conventional MACD structure and the filtered
//   Impulse framework.
// • Disagreement can show that one momentum model is expanding or rolling over before the other.
// • The indicator is therefore designed as a comparison / context tool, not as an attempt to make the two
//   MACD families mathematically identical.
//
// DEVELOPING AUTO-NEXT-HTF MACD HIST
// • A Developing higher-timeframe MACD Histogram is calculated natively on the automatically selected next HTF.
// • The higher-timeframe engine recalculates the complete selected MACD Fast / Slow / Signal lengths and its own
//   ATR14 inside that HTF context before applying NMS.
// • It is NOT a resampled chart-timeframe histogram.
// • Transport uses gaps_off + lookahead_off with no confirmed-bar [1] offset.
// • The result is deliberately DEVELOPING and can continue changing until the active higher-timeframe candle closes.
// • This provides immediate context for whether the current chart-timeframe histogram is aligned with, diverging
//   from, or moving ahead of the developing momentum structure one timeframe above.
//
// DISPLAY ARCHITECTURE
// • MACD / Signal = foreground pair; default Line / Width 1 / Transparency 65.
// • Impulse MACD / Signal = contextual backdrop pair; both default Line / Width 1 / Transparency 65.
// • MACD Hist and Impulse Hist default Histogram.
// • Developing HTF MACD Hist defaults Line so it can be read as context without becoming a third competing histogram.
// • MACD / Signal and Impulse MACD / Signal each have independent fill controls.
// • The entire MACD family shares one user-adjustable Bull / Bear / Neutral palette:
//      MACD / Signal plots, fill, MACD Hist, Developing HTF MACD Hist, and right labels.
// • The entire Impulse family shares one user-adjustable Bull / Bear / Neutral palette:
//      Impulse MACD / Signal plots, fill, Impulse Hist, and right labels.
// • Transparency remains independently adjustable by visual layer.
// • Line / Columns / Histogram presentation is available where applicable.
// • Default Last N = 144 across the primary displayed families.
// • Historical plot / fill windows use native show_last.
//
// PRICE-PANE COMPANION
// • Optional force-overlay candles plot the chart's actual Open / High / Low / Close on the main price pane.
// • Candle / follow-line color source:
//      MACD Hist = DEFAULT;
//      Impulse Hist.
// • The selected histogram supplies COLOR only; candle geometry remains native chart OHLC.
// • Candle transparency defaults:
//      Body = 75;
//      Wick = 0;
//      Border = 0.
// • A lightweight Close bar-to-bar follow line is always force-overlaid using the same selected histogram color.
// • The follow line is intentionally hardcoded to Last N 2 / Width 1 / Transparency 0.
// • No additional momentum kernels are created; the price-pane companion reuses existing histogram state colors.
//
// FOCUSED NMS GUIDES
// • Guide ladder:
//      -100 / -89 / -75 / -55 / -34 / -13 / 0 / 13 / 34 / 55 / 75 / 89 / 100.
// • Zero remains the fixed center reference.
// • Non-zero guides are proximity-gated against the CURRENTLY VISIBLE plotted geometry:
//      MACD / Signal,
//      MACD Hist,
//      Developing HTF MACD Hist,
//      Impulse MACD / Signal,
//      Impulse Hist.
// • A guide is shown only when at least one visible plotted value is genuinely close to that NMS rung.
// • Capture radius = max(6 NMS points, 35% of that rung's nearest ladder spacing).
// • This avoids filling the pane with distant levels such as ±55 / ±75 when no visible momentum series is
//   actually approaching those areas.
// • ±100 additionally requires visible plotted geometry beyond ±95.
// • Guide COLORS remain MACD-state colors; guide VISIBILITY responds to all visible momentum geometry.
// • Guide labels default SHOW; guide lines remain optional.
//
// RIGHT-SIDE TELEMETRY
// • One dynamic First Label Padding / Padding Between Labels system manages all right-side telemetry.
// • Padding modes:
//      Individual = DEFAULT;
//      Grouped = all visible telemetry labels share the first-padding lane.
// • Individual order:
//      Guide Levels
//      → MACD Hist
//      → MACD
//      → MACD Signal
//      → Developing HTF MACD Hist
//      → Impulse Hist
//      → Impulse MACD
//      → Impulse Signal.
// • Only visible labels consume Individual spacing.
// • No forward bar_index offsets are used.
// • MACD / Signal and Impulse MACD / Signal crossover ages are inclusive:
//      the crossover bar itself = 1ba.
// • Crossover age follows directional ownership:
//      Bull state → ba on MACD / Impulse MACD;
//      Bear state → ba on the corresponding Signal label.
//
// HOW TO READ IT
// • Start with sign:
//      above 0 = positive signed momentum;
//      below 0 = negative signed momentum.
// • Then look at pair ownership:
//      MACD above Signal or Impulse MACD above Signal indicates the faster momentum component currently leads.
// • Then look at magnitude on NMS:
//      a move from 13 → 34 is materially different from 55 → 75 because the outer scale requires progressively
//      larger ATR-relative expansion.
// • Use the histograms to judge the current distance between each MACD family and its Signal.
// • Use the Developing HTF MACD Hist to compare local histogram direction / magnitude with the next timeframe.
// • Read agreement, disagreement, expansion, contraction, and crossover age together rather than treating any
//   single NMS level as a standalone trading signal.
//
// IMPORTANT
// • The Normalized Momentum Scale is a descriptive momentum coordinate, not a prediction model.
// • It does not change the underlying MACD / Signal relationships; it changes how their volatility-relative
//   magnitude is represented so multiple momentum families can be compared in one bounded pane.
// • All calculations remain derived from historical / developing market data and should be used as context,
//   not as a guarantee of future price direction.
//
// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Script Overview
// ==============================================================================================

// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Constants
// ==============================================================================================

// 🔹 Display vocabulary
const string SHOW = "Show"
const string HIDE = "Hide"
const string STYLE_LINE = "Line"
const string STYLE_COLUMNS = "Columns"
const string STYLE_HISTOGRAM = "Histogram"
const string GUIDE_LABELS = "Labels Only"
const string GUIDE_BOTH = "Lines + Labels"
const string GUIDE_HIDE = "Hide"
const string LABEL_PADDING_GROUPED = "Grouped"
const string LABEL_PADDING_INDIVIDUAL = "Individual"

const string PRICE_SOURCE_MACD_HIST = "MACD Hist"
const string PRICE_SOURCE_IMPULSE_HIST = "Impulse Hist"

// 🔹 Input groups
const string G_MACD = "01 — MACD / Signal"
const string G_HIST = "02 — MACD Histogram"
const string G_IMPULSE = "03 — Impulse / Signal"
const string G_GUIDES = "04 — Focused Guides"
const string G_RIGHT_LABELS = "05 — Right-Side Labels"
const string G_PRICE_OVERLAY = "06 — Price Pane Overlay"

// 🔹 Price MACD defaults
const int MACD_FAST_LEN_DEFAULT = 12
const int MACD_SLOW_LEN_DEFAULT = 26
const int MACD_SIGNAL_LEN_DEFAULT = 9

// 🔹 Canonical LazyBear Impulse defaults
const int IMPULSE_MA_LEN_DEFAULT = 34
const int IMPULSE_SIGNAL_LEN_DEFAULT = 9

// 🔹 Shared volatility normalization
const int ATR_LEN = 14
const int PAIR_LAST_N_DEFAULT = 144

// 🔹 Canonical pair palette
const color COL_BULL = color.teal
const color COL_BEAR = #f51673
const color COL_NEUTRAL = color.rgb(165, 165, 165)

// 🔹 Impulse Histogram palette
const color COL_IMPULSE_HIST_BULL = #ff8400
const color COL_IMPULSE_HIST_BEAR = color.rgb(157, 78, 221)

// 🔹 Focused guide palette
const color COL_GUIDE_POS_PENDING = color.teal
const color COL_GUIDE_POS_PASSED = #ffe102
const color COL_GUIDE_NEG_BELOW = #f51673
const color COL_GUIDE_NEG_PASSED = color.rgb(165, 165, 165)
const color COL_GUIDE_ZERO = color.rgb(165, 165, 165)
const color COL_POS_EXTREME = #f76300
const color COL_NEG_EXTREME = #7a00a0

// 🔹 Focused guide proximity + line defaults
const float GUIDE_PROXIMITY_FLOOR = 6.0
const float GUIDE_PROXIMITY_FRACTION = 0.35
const int GUIDE_LINE_LAST_N_DEFAULT = 2
const int GUIDE_LINE_WIDTH_DEFAULT = 1

// 🔹 Hardcoded price-pane follow-line baseline
const int PRICE_FOLLOW_LAST_N = 2
const int PRICE_FOLLOW_WIDTH = 1
const int PRICE_FOLLOW_TRANSP = 0

const float DIRECTION_EPS = 1e-8

// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Constants
// ==============================================================================================

// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Tooltips
// ==============================================================================================

// 🔹 MACD / Signal explanation
const string TT_MACD =
     "PRICE MACD / SIGNAL — NORMALIZED MOMENTUM SCALE\n\n" +
     "Default raw MACD = EMA12(Close) − EMA26(Close). Signal = EMA9(raw MACD). Fast / Slow / Signal lengths are user-adjustable.\n\n" +
     "Each raw line is divided by ATR14 and independently passed through the fixed Normalized Momentum Scale transfer. " +
     "This preserves true crossover/order while placing both lines on a bounded -100…+100 volatility-relative coordinate.\n\n" +
     "MACD > Signal uses the shared Bull color. Signal > MACD uses the shared Bear color. The same Bull / Bear / Neutral palette drives both the MACD / Signal plots and their fill; fill transparency remains independent.\n\n" +
     "Display Style controls both pair members. Last N uses native show_last."

// 🔹 MACD Histogram explanation
const string TT_HIST =
     "ACTUAL MACD HISTOGRAM — NORMALIZED MOMENTUM SCALE\n\n" +
     "Raw Histogram = raw MACD − raw Signal.\n\n" +
     "The raw histogram is divided by ATR14 and passed through Normalized Momentum Scale independently. " +
     "It is NOT calculated by subtracting the already-remapped semantic MACD and Signal lines, because that would distort magnitude after the nonlinear transfer.\n\n" +
     "The MACD Histogram inherits the shared MACD Bull / Bear / Neutral palette."

// 🔹 Developing HTF MACD Histogram explanation
const string TT_HTF_HIST =
     "DEVELOPING AUTO-NEXT-HTF MACD HISTOGRAM — NMS\n\n" +
     "The complete Price MACD Histogram is calculated natively on the automatically selected next higher timeframe:\n" +
     "EMA12(Close) − EMA26(Close) → EMA9 Signal → raw Histogram → ÷ native HTF ATR14 → Normalized Momentum Scale.\n\n" +
     "Transport uses gaps_off + lookahead_off with no [1] confirmed-bar offset. This is a developing HTF reading, so its value can continue changing until the active higher-timeframe candle closes.\n\n" +
     "Default presentation = Line / SHOW, Last N = 144. The Developing HTF Histogram inherits the shared MACD Bull / Bear / Neutral palette. The right label shows the actual selected HTF."

// 🔹 Impulse / Signal explanation
const string TT_IMPULSE =
     "IMPULSE MACD / SIGNAL — NORMALIZED MOMENTUM SCALE\n\n" +
     "LazyBear ownership:\n" +
     "• ImpulseMACD = md.\n" +
     "• Signal = sb = SMA(md, Signal Length).\n" +
     "• Impulse Hist = sh = md − sb.\n\n" +
     "Default source architecture = HLC3 + SMMA/RMA34 High/Low envelope + ZLEMA34 midline. MA Length and Signal Length are user-adjustable. " +
     "ImpulseMACD measures how far the ZLEMA extends outside the smoothed High/Low envelope; zero means the midline remains inside the envelope.\n\n" +
     "Raw ImpulseMACD and Signal are each divided by ATR14 and independently passed through the SAME fixed Normalized Momentum Scale transfer as Price MACD / Signal.\n\n" +
     "DEFAULT PRESENTATION:\n" +
     "• ImpulseMACD = Histogram.\n" +
     "• Impulse Signal = Line.\n" +
     "• Impulse Hist = Histogram / SHOW.\n\n" +
     "ImpulseMACD > Signal uses the shared Impulse Bull color. Signal > ImpulseMACD uses the shared Impulse Bear color. The same Bull / Bear / Neutral palette drives the Impulse plots, fill, histogram, and right labels."

// 🔹 Impulse Histogram explanation
const string TT_IMPULSE_HIST =
     "IMPULSEHISTO — LAZYBEAR sh = md − sb — NORMALIZED MOMENTUM SCALE\n\n" +
     "This is the original LazyBear Impulse Hist relationship: sh = md − sb, where md is ImpulseMACD and sb is its SMA9 Signal.\n\n" +
     "The raw Impulse histogram is divided by ATR14 and passed through Normalized Momentum Scale independently. " +
     "It is NOT calculated by subtracting the already-remapped semantic Impulse and Signal values.\n\n" +
     "The Impulse Histogram inherits the shared Impulse Bull / Bear / Neutral palette. Defaults remain orange bullish, light purple bearish, and neutral gray.\n\n" +
     "The Impulse histogram renders behind the standard MACD histogram and shares the Impulse Last-N window."

// 🔹 Focused guides
const string TT_GUIDES =
     "FOCUSED SEMANTIC GUIDES\n\n" +
     "Zero always remains available as the center reference. Non-zero guide visibility is based on proximity to the CURRENTLY VISIBLE plotted geometry — MACD / Signal, MACD Hist, Developing HTF MACD Hist, ImpulseMACD / Signal, and Impulse Hist.\n\n" +
     "A guide appears only when at least one visible plotted value is genuinely close to that semantic rung. Capture radius = max(6 semantic points, 35% of the rung's nearest ladder spacing). This prevents distant ±55 / ±75 guides from appearing simply because they are the next rungs beyond MACD.\n\n" +
     "Guide levels = 0 / ±13 / ±34 / ±55 / ±75 / ±89 / ±100. ±100 additionally requires visible plotted geometry beyond ±95.\n\n" +
     "Guide COLORS remain MACD-state colors; only guide VISIBILITY uses all visible geometry. Labels Only is the default. Lines + Labels adds short right-edge dotted/dashed guide segments."

// 🔹 Price-pane overlay
const string TT_PRICE_OVERLAY =
     "PRICE PANE OVERLAY\n\n" +
     "Plots actual chart OHLC on the main price pane with force_overlay=true while this indicator remains in its oscillator pane.\n\n" +
     "Color Source:\n" +
     "• MACD Hist = candle / follow-line color follows the sign of the standard MACD Histogram.\n" +
     "• Impulse Hist = candle / follow-line color follows the sign of the Impulse Histogram.\n\n" +
     "The default source is MACD Hist. Candle body / wick / border transparency are independently adjustable.\n\n" +
     "A hardcoded Close bar-to-bar follow line also uses the selected histogram color source. It always shows only the most recent 2 bars."

const string TT_PRICE_CANDLE_TRANSP =
     "Independent transparency controls for the force-overlay price candles.\n\n" +
     "Defaults:\n" +
     "• Body = 75\n" +
     "• Wick = 0\n" +
     "• Border = 0"

// 🔹 Canonical padding
const string TT_PADDING =
     "One dynamic right-label padding engine.\n\n" +
     "Individual — DEFAULT. Every visible telemetry label owns its own horizontal lane.\n" +
     "Grouped — all visible telemetry labels share the first-padding lane.\n\n" +
     "Order: Guide Levels → MACD Histogram → MACD → MACD Signal → HTF MACD Histogram → Impulse Hist → ImpulseMACD → Impulse Signal.\n\n" +
     "All active guide rungs remain one Guide family. First Label Padding controls the first visible lane. " +
     "Padding Between Labels controls the standard distance to each next visible label in Individual mode. " +
     "A +2 EM visual compensation is applied after ImpulseMACD so the wider Impulse pair does not crowd its neighbor. " +
     "Only visible labels consume spacing.\n\n" +
     "No forward bar_index offset is used."

// ==============================================================================================
// 🔴 END REGION: Tooltips
// ==============================================================================================

// ==============================================================================================
// 🟢 REGION: Inputs
// ==============================================================================================

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: MACD / Signal Foreground
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// 🔹 Calculation lengths
int in_macdFastLen = input.int(MACD_FAST_LEN_DEFAULT, "MACD Fast Length", minval=1, maxval=500, group=G_MACD, tooltip=TT_MACD)
int in_macdSlowLen = input.int(MACD_SLOW_LEN_DEFAULT, "MACD Slow Length", minval=1, maxval=500, group=G_MACD, tooltip=TT_MACD)
int in_macdSignalLen = input.int(MACD_SIGNAL_LEN_DEFAULT, "MACD Signal Length", minval=1, maxval=500, group=G_MACD, tooltip=TT_MACD)

// 🔹 Pair presentation
string in_macdDisplayMode = input.string(SHOW, "MACD / Signal Display", options=[SHOW, HIDE], group=G_MACD, tooltip=TT_MACD)
bool showMacdPair = in_macdDisplayMode == SHOW
string in_macdStyle = input.string(STYLE_LINE, "  ↳ Display Style", options=[STYLE_LINE, STYLE_COLUMNS, STYLE_HISTOGRAM], group=G_MACD, active=showMacdPair, tooltip=TT_MACD)
int in_macdLastN = input.int(PAIR_LAST_N_DEFAULT, "  ↳ Last N Bars", minval=1, maxval=5000, group=G_MACD, active=showMacdPair)
int in_macdWidth = input.int(1, "  ↳ Width", minval=1, maxval=5, group=G_MACD, active=showMacdPair)
int in_macdTransp = input.int(65, "  ↳ Plot Transparency", minval=0, maxval=100, group=G_MACD, active=showMacdPair)

// 🔹 Shared MACD / Signal plot + fill colors
color in_macdBullColor = input.color(COL_BULL, "Bull", group=G_MACD, inline="macdSharedColors")
color in_macdBearColor = input.color(COL_BEAR, "Bear", group=G_MACD, inline="macdSharedColors")
color in_macdNeutralColor = input.color(COL_NEUTRAL, "Neutral", group=G_MACD, inline="macdSharedColors")

// 🔹 Pair fill
string in_macdFillMode = input.string(SHOW, "MACD / Signal Fill", options=[SHOW, HIDE], group=G_MACD, tooltip=TT_MACD)
bool showMacdFill = in_macdFillMode == SHOW
int in_macdFillTransp = input.int(75, "  ↳ Fill Transparency", minval=0, maxval=100, group=G_MACD, active=showMacdFill)

// 🔹 Pair right labels
string in_macdRightLabelsMode = input.string(SHOW, "MACD / Signal Right-Side Labels", options=[SHOW, HIDE], group=G_MACD)
bool showMacdRightLabels = in_macdRightLabelsMode == SHOW

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Actual MACD Histogram
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// 🔹 Histogram presentation
string in_histDisplayMode = input.string(SHOW, "MACD Histogram Display", options=[SHOW, HIDE], group=G_HIST, tooltip=TT_HIST)
bool showMacdHist = in_histDisplayMode == SHOW
string in_histStyle = input.string(STYLE_HISTOGRAM, "  ↳ Display Style", options=[STYLE_LINE, STYLE_COLUMNS, STYLE_HISTOGRAM], group=G_HIST, active=showMacdHist, tooltip=TT_HIST)
int in_histLastN = input.int(PAIR_LAST_N_DEFAULT, "  ↳ Last N Bars", minval=1, maxval=5000, group=G_HIST, active=showMacdHist)
int in_histWidth = input.int(2, "  ↳ Width", minval=1, maxval=5, group=G_HIST, active=showMacdHist)
int in_histTransp = input.int(35, "  ↳ Transparency", minval=0, maxval=100, group=G_HIST, active=showMacdHist)

// 🔹 Histogram right label
string in_histRightLabelMode = input.string(SHOW, "MACD Histogram Right-Side Label", options=[SHOW, HIDE], group=G_HIST)
bool showMacdHistRightLabel = in_histRightLabelMode == SHOW

// 🔹 Developing Auto-Next-HTF MACD Histogram
string in_htfHistDisplayMode = input.string(SHOW, "Developing HTF MACD Hist", options=[SHOW, HIDE], group=G_HIST, tooltip=TT_HTF_HIST)
bool showHtfMacdHist = in_htfHistDisplayMode == SHOW
string in_htfHistStyle = input.string(STYLE_LINE, "  ↳ HTF Display Style", options=[STYLE_LINE, STYLE_COLUMNS, STYLE_HISTOGRAM], group=G_HIST, active=showHtfMacdHist, tooltip=TT_HTF_HIST)
int in_htfHistLastN = input.int(PAIR_LAST_N_DEFAULT, "  ↳ HTF Last N Bars", minval=1, maxval=5000, group=G_HIST, active=showHtfMacdHist)
int in_htfHistWidth = input.int(2, "  ↳ HTF Width", minval=1, maxval=5, group=G_HIST, active=showHtfMacdHist)
int in_htfHistTransp = input.int(0, "  ↳ HTF Transparency", minval=0, maxval=100, group=G_HIST, active=showHtfMacdHist)

string in_htfHistRightLabelMode = input.string(SHOW, "HTF MACD Hist Right-Side Label", options=[SHOW, HIDE], group=G_HIST, tooltip=TT_HTF_HIST)
bool showHtfMacdHistRightLabel = in_htfHistRightLabelMode == SHOW

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Impulse / Signal Backdrop
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// 🔹 Calculation lengths
int in_impulseMaLen = input.int(IMPULSE_MA_LEN_DEFAULT, "Impulse MACD MA Length", minval=1, maxval=500, group=G_IMPULSE, tooltip=TT_IMPULSE)
int in_impulseSignalLen = input.int(IMPULSE_SIGNAL_LEN_DEFAULT, "Impulse Signal / Hist Length", minval=1, maxval=500, group=G_IMPULSE, tooltip=TT_IMPULSE)

// 🔹 Pair presentation
string in_impulseDisplayMode = input.string(SHOW, "ImpulseMACD / Signal Display", options=[SHOW, HIDE], group=G_IMPULSE, tooltip=TT_IMPULSE)
bool showImpulsePair = in_impulseDisplayMode == SHOW
string in_impulseMacdStyle = input.string(STYLE_LINE, "  ↳ ImpulseMACD Style", options=[STYLE_LINE, STYLE_COLUMNS, STYLE_HISTOGRAM], group=G_IMPULSE, active=showImpulsePair, tooltip=TT_IMPULSE)
string in_impulseSignalStyle = input.string(STYLE_LINE, "  ↳ Impulse Signal Style", options=[STYLE_LINE, STYLE_COLUMNS, STYLE_HISTOGRAM], group=G_IMPULSE, active=showImpulsePair, tooltip=TT_IMPULSE)
int in_impulseLastN = input.int(PAIR_LAST_N_DEFAULT, "  ↳ Last N Bars", minval=1, maxval=5000, group=G_IMPULSE, active=showImpulsePair)
int in_impulseWidth = input.int(1, "  ↳ Width", minval=1, maxval=5, group=G_IMPULSE, active=showImpulsePair)
int in_impulseTransp = input.int(65, "  ↳ Plot Transparency", minval=0, maxval=100, group=G_IMPULSE, active=showImpulsePair)

// 🔹 Shared Impulse MACD / Signal / Hist plot + fill colors
color in_impulseBullColor = input.color(COL_IMPULSE_HIST_BULL, "Bull", group=G_IMPULSE, inline="impulseSharedColors")
color in_impulseBearColor = input.color(COL_IMPULSE_HIST_BEAR, "Bear", group=G_IMPULSE, inline="impulseSharedColors")
color in_impulseNeutralColor = input.color(COL_NEUTRAL, "Neutral", group=G_IMPULSE, inline="impulseSharedColors")

// 🔹 Pair fill
string in_impulseFillMode = input.string(SHOW, "Impulse / Signal Fill", options=[SHOW, HIDE], group=G_IMPULSE, tooltip=TT_IMPULSE)
bool showImpulseFill = in_impulseFillMode == SHOW
int in_impulseFillTransp = input.int(90, "  ↳ Fill Transparency", minval=0, maxval=100, group=G_IMPULSE, active=showImpulseFill)

// 🔹 Pair right labels
string in_impulseRightLabelsMode = input.string(SHOW, "Impulse / Signal Right-Side Labels", options=[SHOW, HIDE], group=G_IMPULSE)
bool showImpulseRightLabels = in_impulseRightLabelsMode == SHOW

// 🔹 Actual Impulse MACD Histogram
string in_impulseHistDisplayMode = input.string(SHOW, "Impulse Hist Display", options=[SHOW, HIDE], group=G_IMPULSE, tooltip=TT_IMPULSE_HIST)
bool showImpulseHist = in_impulseHistDisplayMode == SHOW
string in_impulseHistStyle = input.string(STYLE_HISTOGRAM, "  ↳ Histogram Style", options=[STYLE_LINE, STYLE_COLUMNS, STYLE_HISTOGRAM], group=G_IMPULSE, active=showImpulseHist, tooltip=TT_IMPULSE_HIST)
int in_impulseHistWidth = input.int(3, "  ↳ Histogram Width", minval=1, maxval=5, group=G_IMPULSE, active=showImpulseHist)
int in_impulseHistTransp = input.int(45, "  ↳ Histogram Transparency", minval=0, maxval=100, group=G_IMPULSE, active=showImpulseHist)

string in_impulseHistRightLabelMode = input.string(SHOW, "Impulse Hist Right-Side Label", options=[SHOW, HIDE], group=G_IMPULSE, tooltip=TT_IMPULSE_HIST)
bool showImpulseHistRightLabel = in_impulseHistRightLabelMode == SHOW

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Focused Semantic Guides
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// 🔹 Focused guide display only
string in_guideMode = input.string(GUIDE_LABELS, "Focused Guide Display", options=[GUIDE_LABELS, GUIDE_BOTH, GUIDE_HIDE], group=G_GUIDES, tooltip=TT_GUIDES)
bool showGuideLabels = in_guideMode != GUIDE_HIDE
bool showGuideLines = in_guideMode == GUIDE_BOTH
bool guideEngineActive = showGuideLabels or showGuideLines

int in_guideLineLastN = input.int(GUIDE_LINE_LAST_N_DEFAULT, "  ↳ Guide Line Last N Bars", minval=1, maxval=5000, group=G_GUIDES, active=showGuideLines)
int in_guideLineWidth = input.int(GUIDE_LINE_WIDTH_DEFAULT, "  ↳ Guide Line Width", minval=1, maxval=5, group=G_GUIDES, active=showGuideLines)
int in_guideLineTransp = input.int(78, "  ↳ Guide Line Transparency", minval=0, maxval=100, group=G_GUIDES, active=showGuideLines)

// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// 🟦 Subregion: Canonical Right-Label Padding
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────

// 🔹 First / spaced construct
string in_rightLabelPaddingMode = input.string(LABEL_PADDING_INDIVIDUAL, "Label Padding Mode", options=[LABEL_PADDING_GROUPED, LABEL_PADDING_INDIVIDUAL], group=G_RIGHT_LABELS, tooltip=TT_PADDING)
bool useGroupedRightLabelPadding = in_rightLabelPaddingMode == LABEL_PADDING_GROUPED
int in_rightLabelBasePad = input.int(2, "First Label Padding", minval=0, maxval=100, group=G_RIGHT_LABELS, tooltip=TT_PADDING)
int in_rightLabelPadStep = input.int(5, "Padding Between Labels", minval=1, maxval=40, group=G_RIGHT_LABELS, tooltip=TT_PADDING)

